  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Capacity Building for Partners and Humanitarian Response in Gaza</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under this six-month project, IOM is contributing to the overall objective of meeting the immediate needs and the alleviation of the suffering of internally displaced persons (IDPs) and other affected people in Gaza through two components of assistance. These build on IOM&#x2019;s extensive technical experience and expertise in emergency humanitarian operations, on-going provision of shelter and non-food items (NFIs) to partners with operations on the ground in Gaza and the expressed priorities of UNRWA in filling gaps in the overall response. IOM is providing technical experts to support technical capacity building on and the overall response under shelter/NFI, water, sanitation and hygiene, and site management areas of intervention. IOM is also procuring, transporting, storing and handing over tarpaulins, ropes and family tents to UNRWA, for onward distribution to affected persons in Gaza.</narrative>
  </description>
